tutorials/dec13
-----------------

The files in this folder (tutorials/dec13) are supporting material for the tutorial given during the 
PANDA Collaboration Meeting in December 2013.

-----------------

General info material about Rho analysis can be found on several Wiki pages:

Standard tutorial: http://panda-wiki.gsi.de/cgi-bin/view/Computing/PandaRootRhoTutorial 
Info Rho Classes : http://panda-wiki.gsi.de/cgi-bin/view/Computing/PandaRootAnalysisJuly13

-----------------

The purpose of this tutorial is to practice several things like e.g.

- principle reconstruction of a decay channel
- doing analysis in a FairTask
- make use of n-Tuples for analysis
- playing around with data

For 

- doing simulation with Box generator, EvtGen or DPM locally or 
- submitting jobs to Prometheus cluster@GSI

please consult README file in macro/prod and/or Wiki page

http://panda-wiki.gsi.de/cgi-bin/view/Computing/PandaRootSimulationPrometheus

-----------------

The files in this directory are:

- README            - this file
- TutDec2013.pdf    - slides for the tutorial session

- tut_ana.C         - template macro for analysis of multiple input files
- tut_ana_task.C    - template macro to run analysis task with multiple input files
- PndTutAnaTask.h   - analysis task template header
- PndTutAnaTask.cxx - analysis task template implementation

- CMakeLists.txt    - necessary to build library
- tutDec13LinkDef.h - necessary to build library

- examples_D0toKpi  - directory with example analysis D0 -> K- pi+ (+c.c.)

-----------------

Reconstructable data for several signal decay channels and DPM are located at

/hera/panda/tutdata/<prefix>/<prefix>_<pbarmom>GeV_<num>_pid.root, <prefix>_<num>_par.root

---------------------------------------------------------
  <prefix>  :   p(pbar)   :  sqrt(s)  :  channel
---------------------------------------------------------

DPM         :    15.15    :    5.5    :    DPM events; to be used as background events 
                                           DPM_15GeV_[1..20]_pid.root, par file DPM_15GeV_1_par.root

D0Kpi       :    15.15    :    5.5    :    D0 D*0, one D0 -> K- pi+; 
                                           D0Kpi_15GeV_[1..10]_pid.root, par file D0Kpi_15GeV_1_par.root

DpmKpipi    :    15.15    :    5.5    :    D+- D*-+, one D+- -> K-+ pi+- pi+-; 
                                           DpmKpipi_15GeV_[1..10]_pid.root, par file DpmKpipi_15GeV_1_par.root
 
DpmKSpipi0  :    15.15    :    5.5    :    D+- D*-+, one D+- -> K_S(pi+ pi-) pi pi0 (gamma gamma) ; 
                                           DpmKSpipi0_15GeV_[1..10]_pid.root, par file DpmKSpipi0_15GeV_1_par.root  

EtacKKpi0   :    15.15    :    5.5    :    eta_c pi+ pi-, eta_c -> K+ K- pi0; 
                                           EtacKKpi0_15GeV_[1..10]_pid.root, par file EtacKKpi0_15GeV_1_par.root  

Jpsi2e      :    15.15    :    5.5    :    J/psi pi+ pi-, J/psi -> e+ e-; 
                                           Jpsi2e_15GeV_[1..10]_pid.root, par file Jpsi2e_15GeV_1_par.root  

LamcPKpi    :    15.15    :    5.5    :    Lambda_c Lambda_c bar, one Lambda_c -> p K- pi+; 
                                           LamcPKpi_15GeV_[1..10]_pid.root, par file LamcPKpi_15GeV_1_par.root  

LamPpi      :    15.15    :    5.5    :    Lambda Lambda bar, one Lambda -> p pi-; 
                                           LamPpi_15GeV_[1..10]_pid.root, par file LamPpi_15GeV_1_par.root  

MuMu        :    15.15    :    5.5    :    pbar p -> mu+ mu-; 
                                           MuMu_15GeV_[1..10]_pid.root, par file MuMu_15GeV_1_par.root  

PhiPhi      :    15.15    :    5.5    :    phi phi, one phi -> K+ K-; 
                                           PhiPhi_15GeV_[1..10]_pid.root, par file PhiPhi_15GeV_1_par.root  







